# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. `gmail_app_password` and `embed_api_key` live here; the versioned
# file is config.example.json. Env vars are the other way in, so .env too.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
config.json
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The index. Everything here is derived from your mailbox: warm vectors
# (hundreds of MB), the preview sidecar and its WAL/SHM, the `--db` baselines
# the README measures against, and a prune's `.bak`. None of it belongs in
# history, and all of it is reproducible with `index` / `reindex` / `media`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal
*.sqlite-journal
*.bak
*.old

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run output. the GUI tails a Refresh into <db>.index.log; `bench`, `reindex`
# and `audit` are otherwise redirected with `>` into a file, and those files
# (final-*.json, demote-*.json, baseline-*-*.json) are the scratch the README's
# numbers were read off — the numbers are in the README, the dumps are not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
/final-*.json
/demote-*.json
/baseline-*-*.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Eval sets. eval/eval.jsonl carries real subject lines and Message-IDs of a
# real mailbox, so it stays local by default; eval/eval.example.jsonl is the
# shape and is tracked. Rebuild the curated set with eval/curation.py.
# Want it in history anyway: git add -f eval/eval.jsonl
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
eval/eval.jsonl
eval/eval.proposed.jsonl

# Scratch input for a manual probe run (test_embed_media.py --image ...)
/testImage.jpg

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python. Byte-code beside the sources, the usual caches, and any venv — the
# real install path is `uv tool install` from the git URL in the README;
# requirements.txt stays the checkout’s editable install.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.coverage.xml
.tox/
.nox/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
pip-log.txt
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# A wheel unpacked beside the code so the mail view can run without touching
# site-packages (`PYTHONPATH=.deps`). `uv tool install` is the real path.
.deps/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS and editor droppings. `.cursorignore` is tracked on purpose; `.cursor/`
# (rules) is not ignored, so committing rules stays possible.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.Spotlight-V100
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
